# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the TanStack Start project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Package Added**: `@vercel/speed-insights@^2.0.0`
- **Method**: Installed using bun package manager
- **Files Modified**: 
  - `package.json` - Added dependency
  - `bun.lock` - Updated lock file with new package and dependencies

### 2. Component Integration
- **File Modified**: `src/routes/__root.tsx`
- **Changes**:
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/react";`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the `RootShell` function's body element, placed after `<Scripts />` component

### 3. Implementation Details
The implementation follows the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation for React applications:
- Retrieved latest instructions from: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Used the React-specific package: `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- Placed the component in the root shell component to ensure it loads on all pages
- The component is positioned at the end of the body to avoid blocking page rendering

### 4. Verification
✅ Build completed successfully without errors
✅ Tests passed (1/1 test suites)
✅ No new linting errors introduced (only pre-existing formatting issues in other files)
✅ Lock file properly updated with all dependencies

## Framework Compatibility
This project uses TanStack Start (React-based), and the integration follows the recommended pattern for React applications by:
- Using the `/react` export from the Speed Insights package
- Adding the component to the root HTML shell for global coverage
- Preserving existing code structure and functionality

## Next Steps
Once deployed to Vercel:
1. The Speed Insights tracking script will automatically be injected
2. Performance metrics will be collected from real user traffic
3. Data can be viewed in the Vercel dashboard under Speed Insights

## Notes
- The component will only track performance metrics in production environments on Vercel
- No API keys or additional configuration needed
- The implementation is non-blocking and won't affect page load performance
